					<div class="col-lg-7 col-sm-12 mb-12">
						<div class="card-body">
							<!-- what -->
							<nav class="navbar navbar-dark text-white bg-info" style="border-radius: 10px 10px 0px 0px;font-weight: bold;">
								What PertOrg can do?
							</nav>
							<div class="card mb-3" style="border-radius: unset;border: 1px solid #ababab;">
								<div class="card-header">Functions of PertOrg 1.0</div>
								<div class="card-body">
									<!-- <h5 class="card-title">Secondary card title</h5> -->
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<!-- <img src="/pertorg_static/img/home_img/home_right_direct.svg" /> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Users can easily search various types of gene perturbations for a model organism using "search" and "browse" functions.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<!-- <img src="/pertorg_static/img/home_img/home_right_direct.svg" /> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Users can compare their gene list with PertOrg signatures, to identify potentially perturbed genes or GMO models in their system using the "analysis" function.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											In brief, users can link gene perturbations with differentially expressed genes, pathways, cell types, tissues, phenotypes and diseases to interrogate gene function, tissue development, phenogenesis, disease mechanism, and disease models, and to assess therapeutic targets and potential gene therapy.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row">
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Perform property concentration analysis on drug set.</p>
									</div> -->
								</div>
								<div class="card-header">Features of PertOrg 1.0</div>
								<div class="card-body">
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											The large number of datasets from multiple <em>in vivo</em> perturbed model organisms.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Genetic perturbation induced changes at multiple levels, i.e. gene/pathway/cell type/phenotype.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row"> -->
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											scRNA-Seq data comparison between before and after perturbation.</p>
									<!-- </div> -->
									<!-- <div class="row">
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Pharmacokinetic/Toxicokinetic/Dosage analysis of a drug set</p>
									</div>
									<div class="row">
										<p class="card-text">
											<span class="mark-symbol">></span>
											Drug screening and drug design</p>
									</div> -->
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
